# Copy this file to .env.deploy and edit it for your server.
# .env.deploy is intentionally ignored by git.

APP_NAME=vibes
DEPLOY_USER=root
DEPLOY_HOST=203.0.113.10
DEPLOY_DOMAIN=vibes.example.com
DEPLOY_PATH=/var/www/vibes
SERVICE_NAME=vibes
SERVICE_HOST=127.0.0.1
SERVICE_PORT=3136
DEPLOY_URL=https://vibes.example.com/healthz

# Optional: pin HTTPS smoke checks to an IP while DNS is propagating.
# DEPLOY_RESOLVE_IP=203.0.113.10

# --- Profile-icon storage ------------------------------------------------------
# Where generated avatar PNGs are stored and how their public URLs are built.
# These are *runtime* values read by the relay; set them in the host's
# server/.env.local (alongside VIBES_ADMIN_PASSWORD) rather than committing them.
# The filesystem store writes to VIBES_AVATAR_DIR (served by the nginx
# /avatars/ alias) and builds URLs from VIBES_AVATAR_BASE_URL.
#
#   VIBES_AVATAR_STORE=filesystem            # 'filesystem' (default) | 's3'
#   VIBES_AVATAR_DIR=/var/www/vibes/avatars  # on-disk dir, outside server/
#   VIBES_AVATAR_BASE_URL=https://vibes.example.com/avatars
#
# The 's3' store is a stub until R2/S3 credentials are wired (VIBES_S3_*).

# --- Admin area (runtime secret, NOT set here) ---------------------------------
# The web admin at /admin is gated by VIBES_ADMIN_PASSWORD. It is a *runtime*
# secret read by the running relay, so it does not belong in this deploy file.
# Put it in a root-only env file on the host that the systemd unit loads:
#
#   install -m 600 /dev/null /var/www/vibes/server/.env.local
#   echo 'VIBES_ADMIN_PASSWORD=<long random value>' >> /var/www/vibes/server/.env.local
#   systemctl restart vibes.service
#
# Leave it unset to keep /admin disabled (returns 404).
